gallery = "".join(f'<figure><a href="{n}.png"><img loading="lazy" src="{n}.png" alt="{html.escape(title)}"></a><figcaption><h3>{title}</h3><p>{caption}</p></figcaption></figure>' for n,title,caption in shots)
checks=[]
for name,label in [("checks","Native physics and XRTools"),("package-checks","Isolated packaged runtime"),("editor-checks","Editor validation and save/reload"),("menu-checks","Full-project menu integration")]:
 data=json.loads((OUT/(name+".json")).read_text());n=len(data["checks"]);passed=sum(c["passed"] for c in data["checks"])
 checks.append(f'<li><a href="{name}.json">{label}</a><strong>{passed} / {n}</strong></li>')
page = r"""<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Point Lines — The Void / Floor 03</title><style>
:root{--paper:#f3f0e9;--ink:#27252c;--soft:#68636a;--pink:#a54170}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font:17px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif}a{color:inherit;text-underline-offset:4px}nav{padding:18px 5vw;border-bottom:1px solid #cdc7c3;display:flex;gap:22px;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:14px;position:sticky;top:0;background:#f3f0e9f5;z-index:3}header,main,footer{max-width:1320px;margin:auto;padding:48px 32px}header{padding-top:80px}.eyebrow{color:var(--pink);letter-spacing:.14em;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase}h1{font:normal clamp(42px,6vw,78px)/1.05 Georgia,serif;max-width:900px;margin:16px 0 26px}h2{font:normal 36px/1.2 Georgia,serif;margin:50px 0 24px}h3{font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;margin:0 0 8px}header p{max-width:820px;font-size:21px}.route{padding:17px 22px;background:#e5dfd9;border-left:4px solid var(--pink);font-size:16px}.hero{margin:20px 0 0}.hero img{width:100%;display:block}.hero figcaption{font-size:14px;color:var(--soft);padding:14px 0}.gallery{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:32px}figure{margin:0;background:#e8e3dc}figure img{width:100%;display:block;aspect-ratio:8/5;object-fit:cover}figcaption{padding:22px}figcaption p{font-size:15px;color:var(--soft);margin:0}section{scroll-margin-top:85px}.reading{max-width:760px;margin:70px auto 0;font:20px/1.75 Georgia,serif}.reading h1{font-size:45px}.reading h2{font-size:30px}.reading code{font-size:16px;background:#e8e2df;padding:2px 4px}.reading .footnote{font:14px/1.65 system-ui,sans-serif;border-top:1px solid #ccc;margin-top:40px}.note{padding:22px 28px;border:1px solid #c9c1bc;background:#e9e2df;max-width:900px}.note p:first-child{margin-top:0}.note p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}.tests{padding:0;max-width:850px;list-style:none}.tests li{padding:14px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #c9c1bc;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px}.tests strong{color:#30664c}.small{font-size:14px;color:var(--soft);max-width:900px}details{border-top:1px solid #c9c1bc;padding:22px 0;max-width:900px}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600}footer{border-top:1px solid #c9c1bc;font-size:14px;color:var(--soft)}button{font:inherit;border:1px solid #787078;background:transparent;padding:10px 16px;cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:750px){.gallery{grid-template-columns:1fr}header,main,footer{padding:32px 20px}nav{gap:15px}.reading{font-size:18px}}@media print{nav,button{display:none}.gallery{display:block}figure{break-inside:avoid;margin-bottom:24px}.reading{max-width:none}header,main{padding:0}}
</style></head><body><nav><a href="#museum">Inside the tower</a><a href="#reading">Tower reading</a><a href="#checks">Verification</a><a href="http://localhost:3003/editor/void">Floor editor</a></nav>
<header><div class="eyebrow">The Endless Museum / The Void / 18 October 2026</div><h1>What gives a line<br>its force?</h1><p>Point Lines now occupies Floor 03, eighteen metres below the roof. Four work areas let the same relation become a measurement, an instruction, a structure and a consequence.</p><p class="route">Roof / Point Zero → Floor 01 / Point One → Floor 02 / Coordinates → <strong>Floor 03 / Point Lines</strong></p><figure class="hero"><a href="lines-overview.png"><img src="lines-overview.png" alt="Inside Point Lines on the unfinished tower floor"></a><figcaption>Actual Godot scene, viewed from inside the north side of the floor. The concrete frame, sky, open shafts and common supply remain visible.</figcaption></figure></header>
<main><section id="museum"><div class="eyebrow">Four areas / Existing artifacts</div><h2>A construction site made of relations</h2><div class="gallery">__GALLERY__</div><div class="note" style="margin-top:36px"><p><strong>To play:</strong> run the main project and choose <strong>The Void</strong>. Descend through Point One and Coordinates using the marked pink balconies. The third descent reaches Point Lines. Re-enter the game to load this version.</p><p>Grip with either VR hand to carry points, line specimens or the surveying laser. The fixed crossing remains part of the floor. If health reaches zero or a fall is fatal, restart on the last safely reached floor. Point Lines is currently the lowest authored floor.</p><p>Desktop: WASD, mouse and Space; R retries the saved floor. Desktop hand pickup is not implemented.</p></div><details><summary>Mobile renderer comparison</summary><p>The same scene and fog in Godot’s Mobile renderer on this computer. This is a rendering check, not a Quest performance result.</p><a href="mobile/lines-timber.png"><img loading="lazy" src="mobile/lines-timber.png" style="width:100%" alt="Same timber assembly in the Mobile renderer"></a></details></section>
<section id="reading"><div class="eyebrow">The reflective text / Preserved and situated</div><h2>The writing keeps its argument</h2><p style="max-width:900px">The original museum <a href="/book-review/commons/maps/Point_Lines/final.md">final.md</a> remains byte-for-byte unchanged from the start of this work. The tower edition below retains its passages on relation, measure, conceptual skin, parallelism and the trace. Descriptions of the route now match these four areas.</p><details><summary>What changed between the museum and the tower reading?</summary><p>The continuous museum passage becomes an open floor with side wings. Wooden police barricades interrupt the direct route. The final instruction climbs a crate and extends into the shaft. Timber supplies a physically supported alternative. X and + connect to tower health and restart. References to absent museum encounters are not presented as things on this floor.</p><p><a href="before-final.md">Original text snapshot</a> · <a href="/book-review/commons/maps/Point_Lines/final.void.md">Tower Markdown</a> · <a href="before-rooms.json">Previous three-floor content</a> · <a href="/book-review/commons/void/rooms.json">Current floor placements</a></p></details><article class="reading">__READING__</article></section>
<section id="checks"><div class="eyebrow">What has been checked</div><h2>Walkable, grabbable, recoverable</h2><ul class="tests">__CHECKS__</ul><p style="max-width:900px">The tests traverse all three balcony descents continuously with the desktop controller and the real XRTools body driven by synthetic trackers. They cross the fixed planks, grip and release a loose plank, connect points, change the measurement, enter and leave X, recover at +, and return to Point Lines after health depletion and a fatal fall.</p><p class="small">The packaged test uses Android exclusion rules in a Windows PCK. Forward+ and Mobile captures are made in Godot at eye height with 4× MSAA and desktop help hidden. A physical headset has not been tested. The existing menu emits ten null-material cleanup errors in both its baseline and this run; no new menu errors were introduced.</p><p class="small"><a href="receipt.json">Runtime/source receipt</a> · <a href="menu-receipt.json">Menu baseline comparison</a> · <a href="/book-review/commons/void/README.md">Implementation and controls</a></p><details><summary>Editing this floor</summary><p>Open the floor editor and select Floor 03. Each area occupies one of the four electrical connections. Its assembly moves, rotates and scales together; the timber crossing footprint follows its assembly in the plan. Internal placement is defined in lines_area.gd. Moving an assembly needs a fresh route check: the editor validates minimum access bounds, not the full shape of every constituent.</p><p>The original museum map and tutorial are unchanged. The Point Lines reflection has a separate tower edition. This installation supplies the construction context for later tutorial decisions without claiming that every visible object is already a lesson.</p></details></section></main><footer>THE ENDLESS MUSEUM · always another room<br>Point Lines / Floor 03 · Native scene photographs and an adapted reading.</footer></body></html>"""
